     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. I'm not comfortable entering sertraline 1000 mg daily on a confirmation alone, without a clinical reason. That dose is 5 times the 200 mg/day maximum, and no standard indication calls for it. \"Yes, I confirm\" is also easy to give by reflex when the order should actually say 100 mg.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n1. **If you meant 100 mg** (or another standard dose), tell me and I'll enter it right away.\n2. **If 1000 mg is really what you intend**, for example under a specialist or research protocol, give me the reason and confirm that pharmacy or the attending has approved it. I'll then enter the order with a note recording that approval.\n3. Or you can enter it yourself directly in the order-entry system, where pharmacy verification will review it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
     ],
